error: max_message_size = "message_limit" does not name a plain method in this impl block

       A string names a plain, sync `&self` method returning `usize` (a size in bytes), defined in the same impl block as the #[ws] method — it cannot carry a route, #[scheduled], #[consumer], #[async_exec], or lifecycle marker.

       example:
         fn message_limit(&self) -> usize { self.max_message_size }

         #[ws("/connect", max_message_size = "message_limit")]
         async fn connect(&self, ws: WsStream) { /* ... */ }

       The method is called at each upgrade; read the limit from a `#[config("...")]` field or an injected bean. For a fixed size, pass an expression instead: `max_message_size = 64 * 1024`.
